{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413509-how-much-can-sidereal-pattern-spider-fate-editing-change","id":1413509,"title":"How much can Sidereal/Pattern Spider Fate-Editing change?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-14T01:20:17-07:00","id":1413509,"title":"How much can Sidereal/Pattern Spider Fate-Editing change?","content":"I've heard a lot of talk about Getimians potentially being Exalts from versions of Creation that collapsed and were destroyed (among other things). <br /> <br /> Whether or not this is true, I want to incorporate the idea into my game of a rogue sidereal who has taken a strand of information from multiple Looms of Fate across multiple failed creation states. (TL;DR he's 'building a case' for the bureau of fate... the long way). How would I go about explaining the actual metaphysical mechanics of this in game? How does a Sidereal &quot;leave behind&quot; their place in a Loom of Fate and insert themselves into another version of Creation's Loom of Fate? Is it possible for the same Sidereal to assist itself across multiple creations? Creation 1 Sidereal is written into Creation 2's Loom by the Creation 2 version of themselves? It seems like that's a huge problem, though, because you end up with multiple instances of the same Sidereal and the same exaltation. Maybe slightly different due to differences in the Essence makeup (think quark spin or quantum configuration used analogously in our world's physics) from on Creation to another - but still basically the same person and exaltation. How would you account for that?<br /> <br /> Basically, can anyone with greater knowledge of Fate and Sidereals (even if from older editions) give me an idea how this <i>might</i> work? Or am I already onto something with my thoughts? I can't think of any other way a Sidereal can get from one creation to another instance of it without <i>someone</i> being an accomplice and &quot;pasting&quot; their information into the loom of fate of the second creation. I don't know of any Sidereal powers that just let them step out of one &quot;instance&quot; into another - but then, for all I know, the Loom of Fate has &quot;reality partitions&quot; that run multiple instances simultaneously. Maybe I'll go with that in my own story at my table even if it's not &quot;100% Lore Accurate&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> BUT I'd love some lore accurate ideas! Or if you guys have other insights on how a Sidereal, Maiden, Pattern Spider, or god may play with these themes, I'd love to hear them to see if I can make use of them in my game. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4407-loving-the-gorgon","name":"Loving the Gorgon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4407_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T06:02:20-07:00","id":1413546,"title":"","content":"&quot;Same person can't occupy the same space at the same time.&quot; Time Cop (yes my references are dated, Umbrella Academy doesn't quote well)<br /> <br /> I don't think there are any canon answers to your questions.<br /> <br /> I think, but I'm not sure, that Getimians come from possible worlds that never existed, more than alternate realities that are destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T06:28:51-07:00","id":1413551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loving the Gorgon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413509-how-much-can-sidereal-pattern-spider-fate-editing-change#post1413509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard a lot of talk about Getimians potentially being Exalts from versions of Creation that collapsed and were destroyed (among other things).</div> </div> </div> </div>You may have heard it said, but the most current word of dev is that this is not accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would I go about explaining the actual metaphysical mechanics of this in game? </div> </div> </div>You're basically going out into homebrew territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does a Sidereal &quot;leave behind&quot; their place in a Loom of Fate and insert themselves into another version of Creation's Loom of Fate? </div> </div> </div>Creation exists in a place. The Loom of Fate exists in a place. Another Creation would presumably <i>also</i> exist in a place, as would its Loom of Fate-analogue. So, presumably, they'd walk there, or ride a dragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems like that's a huge problem, though, because you end up with multiple instances of the same Sidereal and the same exaltation. </div> </div> </div>Some hold that identity is a lie we all tell ourselves to shut out the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe slightly different due to differences in the Essence makeup (think quark spin or quantum configuration used analogously in our world's physics) from on Creation to another - but still basically the same person and exaltation. How would you account for that? </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Exaltation or not, why is it a problem for there to be two of me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically, can anyone with greater knowledge of Fate and Sidereals (even if from older editions) give me an idea how this <i>might</i> work? </div> </div> </div>In older editions, it doesn't work, because there's just the one Creation. There might exist other worlds out in the Wyld, but they're not Creation. In the current edition, there's nothing that's been written to suggest parallel Creations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't think of any other way a Sidereal can get from one creation to another instance of it without <i>someone</i> being an accomplice and &quot;pasting&quot; their information into the loom of fate of the second creation. </div> </div> </div>Why can't he just walk there? Being &quot;outside of Fate&quot; was a status you could have in previous editions, and still be walking around in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T00:44:14-07:00","id":1413723,"title":"","content":"Getimians aren't from alternate worlds, they're more like from aborted prophecies. Like Heaven has this big plan for where creation is going, and they lay out the plan in strands in the loom of Fate, but Heaven is a big often corrupt bureaucracy and essence users like exalted, demons and ghosts can mess up Fate so the Gods have to abort some of the destinies they have planned out and snip the strands of Fate. Some of these strands were destinies of heroes whose actions would have changed creation in some way, these strands can be merged with a Getimian exaltation to bring this unborn hero into creation, from the Getimian's perspective they woke up in a world in which they were never born and their accomplishments are undone, because they never had a chance to do them in the first place.<br /> <br /> Let's come up with an example: let's say there was a prophecy of this One True King<sup>tm</sup> coming back from an old dynasty to bring a new golden age for this kingdom, then Heaven decides it wants that kingdom to become a satrap of the Realm instead, so they leave the whole One True King<sup>tm </sup>business on the cutting room floor like an early draft. Then some angry sidereal elder says 'screw heaven' makes off with the prophecy, puts an Exaltation in it, next thing you know a Prince who was never born shows up with memories of reclaiming his thrown but no one has ever heard of him or his family, so he set's out to reclaim it (again!) and uses his new powers to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 09-15-2020, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}